    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37759" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ-ώστης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one
				who drives out,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄρης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					322
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἄνεμοι</span> violent winds <i>which
				drive ships ashore</i> (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξωθέω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.113
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>VM</u>
				9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				1.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ἐ.</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφυγμός</span>), term coined by <i><span class="en">
				Archig.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				8.662
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξώστρα</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				111
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cod.Just.</u>
				8.10.12.5b
			</span></i> (pl.), <u>Gloss.</u>
        </div>
